  "body": "Closes #784\nClaim: cloud/i784-sonnet\n\n**Problem.** A lot closed as not planned still showed in the M5 feature cards (above a pill that excluded it), still counted in « débloque N », and « Aussi dans M5 · 0 » rendered as an empty card.\n\n**Change.** `tooling/roadmap/weekly/build.py`: `slide_m5`'s body moves to `m5_cards()` (pure extraction, so it is testable) and lists live lots only; `dependents()` iterates live lots; the dashed card is skipped when empty. No other behaviour change.\n\n**Tests** (`scripts/tests/test_roadmap.py`, real `lots.json`, nothing done, chosen lots dropped): `test_ms_lots_filters_the_dropped_lots`, `test_card_pill_counts_live_lots_only`, `test_left_card_lists_and_counts_live_lots_only`, `test_m5_slide_lists_no_dropped_lot_in_a_feature_card`, `test_m5_slide_drops_the_empty_also_card_and_counts_the_rest`, `test_a_dropped_lot_does_not_count_in_unblocks`. The last three failed before the fix; removing the filter from `card_pill`, `left_card` or `ms_lots` each makes a test fail (checked by mutation). Linux-only change: no macOS job.\n\n**Render check.** Deck rendered with LOT-110, 143, 176 and 183 simulated as not planned: M5 reads 0/21 (25 − 4), the Navigation and Accueil cards show 4 lots, no empty « Aussi » card. No state/image committed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFFmc6Rw3TFH4Q8AUN)_",
