   "updated_at": "2026-11-11T11:21:26Z",
   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5): APPROVE** — head 10b2bccfa59cdf8ed09067722a18d7aabc63d64d\n\n1. **Low**, `tooling/roadmap/weekly/build.py:591`: no test covers the authored lot order. If `key=lambda l: ls.index(lot_n(l))` is replaced by a plain `sorted(...)`, the Navigation card shows 145 before 148, and all 69 tests still pass (checked by mutation). Fix: add one assertion that `m5_cards()` lists the `<li>` items in `FEATURES['M5']` order.\n2. **Low**, `build.py:590-593` and `slide_feature`: this is the same kind of problem as item 4, but in the feature cards. If every lot of a feature is dropped (for example all four lots of « MP et listes »), its card still renders, with an empty `<ul>` and « À faire · 0 lots ». Fix: skip a card with no live lots, or record in #784 that this is accepted.\n3. **Detail**, `build.py:596`: with the « Aussi » card hidden, M5 has 5 cards in a 3-column grid, which leaves one empty cell. `slide_feature` avoids that with `span2`. Fix: give the last card `span2` when `len(cards) % 3 == 2`, or accept the gap.\n\n**Checked**: 69 tests OK; mutations on `card_pill`, `ms_lots`, `left_card`, `dependents`, the M5 card lots and `if rest:` each make a test fail; order unchanged with nothing dropped; no other unfiltered use of `G.rows` / `dependents`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
